  "source_target": "Authored integration ingredient implicit in printed FIRST4.6: real canonical finite KL(r_y||stdGaussian) <= onehalf actual smooth-rho Fisher <= eta² d/2. PrintedE6 itself is W2 <= sqrt Fisher <= eta sqrtposition <= eta sqrt d. The KL inequality is GaussianLSI background, not a printed standalone SPHMC theorem.",
  "semantic_slots": {
    "objects": "True normalized unreflected R_eta,y(dx)∝exp(-V(x)-norm(x-y)²/(2eta))dx; unique p=prox_etaV(y); rho(u)=V(p+sqrteta*u)-V(p)-sqrteta inner(gradV(p),u); r actual inverse-sqrteta affine image; gamma variance1; canonical ENNReal KL and actual smooth-rho gradient squared under SAME r.",
    "domains": "Source R^d, V globallyC2 and kappa^-1 I<=HessV<=I after beta1 normalization; eta>0 fixed,y arbitrary. Actual probability/finite normalizers/finiteKL/positionL2/gradientL2 must be derived; rank0/measurablefamily are explicit authored extensions, not printed standing.",
    "quantifiers": "Universal source V/kappa/positive eta/y; actual characterized p with uniqueness before defining same rho/R/r. Desired numerical KL bound for each same actual law. If extending family: measurable p before all s; no hidden witness-coherence/certificate assumption.",
    "assumptions": "Only source V C2 and global Hessian kappa^-1..1/kappa>=1, eta>0; no eta<=1 or numericalcap1/(2beta), probability/partition/moment/domain/LSI/bound certificates. Numericalcap is separate algorithmic cost contract; Lemma4.1 eta<=1 is neighboring Hessian-smoothing scope.",
    "conclusion": "Canonical KL finite before toReal, actual true standardized law probability/AC, smoothrho score L2 with KL.toReal<=eta² d/2, viahalfFisher+Fishereta²d. Exact future signature still to be compared; no future theorem approval here.",
    "scopes": "Authored coherent integration of source omitted GaussianLSI and true posterior moment obligations. Not proof ofT2/W2/FIRST4.6,bias4.2,MGF4.3/fullLemma/main/cost. Canonical RN equality onlyAE, cannot pointwise differentiate selectedRN. SourceEx9 score/posterior mean identity distinct from Gaussian gradient-output law; noPBPS reflected law or quarter scaling.",
    "constant_dependencies": "stdGaussian variance1; GaussianfunctionLSI2 and sqrt-density energyquarter give KLhalfFisher; source grad rho(0)=0 and etaLip give Fisher<=eta²position; 1stronglylogconcave mode0 gives position<=d. Hence eta²d/2; no κ/dimension-dependent constants besides actuald. Finite realHilbert generalization uses finrank, true Euclidean norm/Riesz gradient, rank0 should yieldKL0."
  },
  "source_gaps": [
    "True Gibbs/RGO normalizers and moment domains; sourcep4.2-p4.3 omit analytic details.",
    "GaussianLSI KL/Fisher adapter with canonical finiteKL and actualsmoothrho; no arbitrary selectedRN pointwise derivative.",
    "Same-p/law/density coherence when joining existential parent producers.",
    "GaussianT2/W2, bias/fullLemma/main/work remain outside leaf."
  ],
  "dependency_vs_binder": "GaussianLSI, integrability, finiteKL, posteriorposition/Fisher moments and same-witness coherence are proof obligations/edges, never additional public assumptions.",
